# THE COMPOSED LAYERS THAT OWE NO SUM, AND FOR WHICH QUANTITY. One row per (composed layer,
# ground), carrying which ground it was and which quantity it lifts.
#
# ⛔⛔⛔ READ `quantity` BEFORE YOU USE THIS. NULL means EVERY quantity is suspended (nobody
#    searched at all); a value means exactly that quantity is (the overlap was found and could
#    not be sized against it). A caller computing one quantity's sum wants
#    `quantity IS NULL OR quantity = '<that one>'`. This file used to claim "no sum at all" while
#    its second arm pinned `demand` and dropped the column, so the claim was true of one arm and
#    false of the other, and nothing downstream could tell.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THIS RELATION EXISTS BECAUSE OF DE MORGAN AND IT IS WORTH SAYING WHY. The condition
#    it replaces was written as a conjunction of two negations, in two different SQL idioms,
#    at two call sites -- an `IS DISTINCT FROM` beside a `NOT EXISTS`. That is the most
#    drift-prone shape there is: two ways to say NOT, neither of which names what is being
#    excluded. `NOT a AND NOT b` is `NOT (a OR b)`, so the thing to name is the DISJUNCTION:
#    the fusions that are suspended. The callers then anti-join one relation, and adding a
#    third ground for suspension is a new file rather than a new clause in two predicates.
#
# ⛔ RUN THIS ALONE BEFORE READING ANY COMPOSITION CHECK. Every row here is a fusion whose
#   arithmetic is not owed, and a checker reporting a pass on one of these rows is reporting
#   about nothing.
-- the two filings that lift the sum rule, each carrying the quantity it lifts.
:union(ALL eliminations/unsearched.sqlc, eliminations/unsized.sqlc)
